# Requirement Authorities: pub

Summary: The scoped authority map for this project. Each subject has at most one active authority, and a scope needed for implementation must have exactly one. Entries stay `unresolved` where evidence is absent; every mapping names a real, checkable location.

| Subject/scope | Authority | Location | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| Observable behavior (current) | unresolved | unresolved | <discover: revision or date> |
| Observable behavior (proposed) | unresolved | unresolved | <discover: revision or date> |
| API contract | <discover: authority or not applicable> | <discover: actual path or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Database/schema | <discover: authority or not applicable> | <discover: actual path or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Configuration keys/defaults | <discover: authority or not applicable> | <discover: actual path or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Go dependencies | `pub` repository | `pub/go.mod` | not applicable |
| Python dependencies | <discover: `pub` repository or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/pyproject.toml` or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/uv.lock` or not applicable> |
| Cargo dependencies | <discover: `pub` repository or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/Cargo.toml` or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/Cargo.lock` or not applicable> |
| Go integration overlay | private meta-repository | `/go.work` | <discover: revision or date> |
| Python integration overlay | private meta-repository | <discover: `/pyproject.toml` + `/uv.lock` or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Cargo integration overlay | private meta-repository | <discover: `/Cargo.toml` or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Build/release implementation | `pub` repository | <discover: Makefile/script/CI path> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Technical decisions | this project's private context | `.agents/context/pub/adr.md` | the register and `decisions/` |
| Execution status | this project's private context | `.agents/context/pub/status.md` | informational only |

## Rules

- Authority is scoped: different subjects may have different authoritative sources without duplication. A local copy never silently becomes a competing specification; link to the authority instead of restating it.
- An entry without evidence stays `unresolved`. A scope needed for the task is resolved before implementation: record what is missing, never a guess.
- Transferring or replacing an authority is the scope owner's change: replace the mapping row and record the evidence in the same review. Superseded locations move into the Evidence column; two active authorities for one scope are always an error.
- A detected specification is a candidate only: detection never confers authority until the owning review confirms it.
- A discrepancy between implementation and the declared authority is reported, not silently normalized. An external authority remains authoritative even when it cannot be fetched; record the gap instead of fabricating its contents.
